      "rev_n_7_f98f26_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_f98f26_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_f98f26",
        "thought_text": "Consider using a binary search approach to find the optimal intersection. Start by setting the initial search range based on the minimum and maximum x and y coordinates of the citizens' houses. For each midpoint in this range, calculate the total distance and check if all citizens are within distance d. Adjust the search range accordingly until the optimal intersection is found or determined to be impossible.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2564346671855668782",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794409246.38022
      },
      "rev_n_8_433368_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_433368_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_433368",
        "thought_text": "Explore using a priority queue (min-heap) to efficiently manage and update the distances of citizens as potential intersection points are considered. This approach could help in dynamically selecting the closest intersection that satisfies the distance constraint d while minimizing the total travel distance.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2564346671855668782",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794409246.3825548
      },
      "rev_n_9_9bb064_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_9bb064_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_9bb064",
        "thought_text": "Implement a sliding window technique over the sorted lists of x and y coordinates to evaluate potential intersections. This method involves maintaining a window of candidate intersections and calculating the total distance for each, ensuring that all citizens are within distance d. This could provide a more systematic way to explore the solution space.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2564346671855668782",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794409246.38256
      },
      "rev_n_10_e2a60b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_e2a60b_0",
        "node_id": "n_10_e2a60b",
        "thought_text": "Re-evaluate the median-based approach by ensuring the median itself is within the distance d for all citizens. The current implementation checks the median but does not verify if all citizens are within d from the median.",
